.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orbit 1  "orbit 0.8.0" 
.SH NAME
orbit \- Orbit from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Orbit from the terminal
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per result, with `"v":1`, instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI colors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
orbit\-login(1)
Sign this device in to a server. The password is read from ORBIT_PASSWORD or stdin
.TP
orbit\-logout(1)
Sign this device out. Unsynced changes wait for the next login
.TP
orbit\-sync(1)
Send queued changes to the server and fetch the rest
.TP
orbit\-status(1)
Show the server, sign\-in state and unsynced count
.TP
orbit\-self\-update(1)
Check for and install a verified CLI release
.TP
orbit\-add(1)
Add a task. Quick\-add syntax applies: dates, p1\-p4, #label, @Area or @project. `\-` reads a list from stdin, one task per line
.TP
orbit\-postpone(1)
Move a task\*(Aqs due date to a phrase, keeping its time unless the phrase gives one
.TP
orbit\-reschedule(1)
Set a task\*(Aqs due date to a phrase, or clear it with `none`. The time is replaced too
.TP
orbit\-snooze(1)
Remind about a task again later: one hour from now by default
.TP
orbit\-overdue(1)
List open tasks whose due date has passed, or move them all with \-\-reschedule
.TP
orbit\-ls(1)
List open tasks in a terminal\-width\-aware table
.TP
orbit\-next(1)
Show what to do next, with a reason for each item
.TP
orbit\-done(1)
Complete a task
.TP
orbit\-show(1)
Show one task
.TP
orbit\-edit(1)
Change a task\*(Aqs title or description
.TP
orbit\-search(1)
Find tasks by words
.TP
orbit\-import(1)
Bring data in from another app
.TP
orbit\-checkin(1)
Check a routine in for a day (default today)
.TP
orbit\-export(1)
Download everything as a zip: items.json, Pages as .md and attachments. With \-\-md, write Areas and Projects as Markdown checklists from this device instead (no server needed)
.TP
orbit\-guide(1)
Print a short reference: commands, refs, listings, JSON shapes and exit codes
.TP
orbit\-mcp(1)
Run as an MCP server over stdio, so AI tools can use Orbit
.TP
orbit\-completions(1)
Print shell completions to stdout
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  orbit add "buy milk"
  orbit ls
  orbit done 1
  orbit guide
.SH VERSION
v0.8.0
